{"id":"77a834d62558f993","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-thm-borsuk-ulam.md","title":"Borsuk–Ulam Theorem","display":"thm-borsuk-ulam — Borsuk–Ulam Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-borsuk-ulam","aliases":["58-thm-borsuk-ulam"],"display":"thm-borsuk-ulam — Borsuk–Ulam Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-continuous-map]]","[[../batch13/58-df-antipodal]]","[[../batch08/58-df-sphere]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-borsuk-ulam"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-borsuk-ulam</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-borsuk-ulam — Borsuk–Ulam Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3cd1834de4f2efb2\" href=\"?note=3cd1834de4f2efb2\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-continuous-map\">../batch19/58-df-continuous-map</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b7e797c34bb8300c\" href=\"?note=b7e797c34bb8300c\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-antipodal\">../batch13/58-df-antipodal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ed44d43cf74ca35e\" href=\"?note=ed44d43cf74ca35e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-sphere\">../batch08/58-df-sphere</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n+1}\\mid \\|x\\|=1\\}\">\\(S^n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n+1}\\mid \\|x\\|=1\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in(\\mathbb{R}^n)^{S^n}\">\\(f\\in(\\mathbb{R}^n)^{S^n}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{S^n}\">\\(\\tau_{S^n}\\)</span> (the Euclidean subspace topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^n\">\\(S^n\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\)</span> (the Euclidean topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Continuous}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Continuous}_S\\)</span> (continuous-map predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Antipodal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Antipodal}_S\\)</span> (antipodal-pair predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S\\)</span> (topology relations defined below)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}euclidean\\text{-}topology\\text{-}for\\text{-}borsuk}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau,m)\n\\leftrightarrow\nm\\in\\omega\\land\n\\tau=\\left\\{U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^m\\,\\middle|\\,\n\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R^m\\;\n(\\|y-x\\|_2&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\right\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}euclidean\\text{-}topology\\text{-}for\\text{-}borsuk}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau,m)\n\\leftrightarrow\nm\\in\\omega\\land\n\\tau=\\left\\{U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^m\\,\\middle|\\,\n\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R^m\\;\n(\\|y-x\\|_2&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\right\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sphere\\text{-}subspace\\text{-}topology}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_S,n)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\n\\exists\\tau_E\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau_E,n+1)\n\\land\\tau_S=\\{U\\cap S^n\\mid U\\in\\tau_E\\}\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sphere\\text{-}subspace\\text{-}topology}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_S,n)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\n\\exists\\tau_E\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau_E,n+1)\n\\land\\tau_S=\\{U\\cap S^n\\mid U\\in\\tau_E\\}\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borsuk\\text{-}ulam}\\ \\vdash\\\nn\\in\\omega\n\\land f\\in(\\mathbb R^n)^{S^n}\n\\land \\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_{S^n},n)\n\\land \\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n},n)\n\\land \\mathrm{Continuous}_S(f,S^n,\\tau_{S^n},\\mathbb R^n,\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n})\n\\to \\exists x,y\\in S^n\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Antipodal}_S(x,y,n)\\land f(x)=f(y)\n\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borsuk\\text{-}ulam}\\ \\vdash\\\nn\\in\\omega\n\\land f\\in(\\mathbb R^n)^{S^n}\n\\land \\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_{S^n},n)\n\\land \\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n},n)\n\\land \\mathrm{Continuous}_S(f,S^n,\\tau_{S^n},\\mathbb R^n,\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n})\n\\to \\exists x,y\\in S^n\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Antipodal}_S(x,y,n)\\land f(x)=f(y)\n\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Borsuk–Ulam: every continuous map from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^n\">\\(S^n\\)</span> to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span> identifies a pair certified by the canonical antipodal predicate.</li>\n<li>The two topology arguments are now fixed to the Euclidean topology and its sphere subspace topology; arbitrary topology parameters would make the statement false or vacuous.</li>\n<li>It has many applications in combinatorics and topology.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-continuous-map","status":"resolved","id":"3cd1834de4f2efb2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-continuous-map]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-antipodal","status":"resolved","id":"b7e797c34bb8300c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-antipodal]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-sphere","status":"resolved","id":"ed44d43cf74ca35e","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-sphere]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"S^n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n+1}\\mid \\|x\\|=1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in(\\mathbb{R}^n)^{S^n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{S^n}","display":false},{"tex":"S^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Continuous}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Antipodal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}euclidean\\text{-}topology\\text{-}for\\text{-}borsuk}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau,m)\n\\leftrightarrow\nm\\in\\omega\\land\n\\tau=\\left\\{U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^m\\,\\middle|\\,\n\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R^m\\;\n(\\|y-x\\|_2<\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U)\\right\\}.","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sphere\\text{-}subspace\\text{-}topology}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_S,n)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\n\\exists\\tau_E\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau_E,n+1)\n\\land\\tau_S=\\{U\\cap S^n\\mid U\\in\\tau_E\\}\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}borsuk\\text{-}ulam}\\ \\vdash\\\nn\\in\\omega\n\\land f\\in(\\mathbb R^n)^{S^n}\n\\land \\mathrm{SphereSubspaceTopology}_S(\\tau_{S^n},n)\n\\land \\mathrm{EuclideanTopology}_S(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n},n)\n\\land \\mathrm{Continuous}_S(f,S^n,\\tau_{S^n},\\mathbb R^n,\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n})\n\\to \\exists x,y\\in S^n\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Antipodal}_S(x,y,n)\\land f(x)=f(y)\n\\bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"S^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false}],"bytes":2210,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4055","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-thm-borsuk-ulam.md|58-thm-borsuk-ulam]]（batch01）"}],"outgoing":["3cd1834de4f2efb2","b7e797c34bb8300c","ed44d43cf74ca35e"]}